==English==
{{was wotd|2008|January|17}}

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*keh₂n-}}
* First attested in 1731.
* {{sense|emphasize}} First attested in 1865.
* From {{der|en|ML.|accentuātus}}, past participle of {{m|la|accentuāre}}, from {{der|en|la|accentus}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/əkˈsɛn.t͡ʃu.eɪt/|/ækˈsɛn.t͡ʃuˌeɪt/|a=RP,US}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-accentuate.ogg|a=US}}
* {{audio|en|en-au-accentuate.ogg|a=AU}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[pronounce]] with an [[accent]] or vocal [[stress]].
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To bring out [[distinctly]]; to make more [[noticeable]] or [[prominent]]; to [[emphasize]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1898|author=w:H. G. Wells|title=s:The War of the Worlds/Book 2/Chapter 3
|passage=our danger and insolation only '''accentuated''' the incompatibility}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1913|author=[[w:Robert Barr (writer)|Robert Barr]]| title=Lord Stranleigh Abroad| chapter=5| url=http://openlibrary.org/works/OL1796924W| passage=These were business hours, and a feeling of loneliness crept over him, perhaps germinated by his sight of the illustrated papers, and '''accentuated''' by an attempted perusal of them.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=1962-03|title=The New Year Freeze-up on British Railways|journal=Modern Railways|page=159|text=Attempts by Waterloo signalmen to clear the points by power operation eventually exhausted point motor batteries, which are fed by trickle chargers, and a blown fuse '''accentuated''' the problem; thus, even when the points had been cleared of ice, no power was available to operate them until the batteries were sufficiently recharged.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1991|publisher=PC World Communications|url=https://books.google.com/books?id=5tASAQAAMAAJ&q=%22stereoizer%22&dq=%22stereoizer%22&hl=en&sa=X&ved=0ahUKEwjRubLWiujVAhXpxFQKHUn2AZ0Q6AEILDAB|journal=Macworld|volume=8
|passage=Several digital effects are supported by Deck, ranging from a digital equalizer, which lets you '''accentuate''' or attenuate certain frequencies, to a stereoizer, which processes a mono- phonic recording to simulate stereo.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2004|author=Mark H Bernstein|title=Without A Tear|publisher=University of Illinois|year_published=2004|page=67
|passage=Eating meat does not conform to God's original intention, and resorting to carnivorism merely '''accentuates''' an unattractive part of human nature.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Vaishnavi Maloth|title=Popular Makeup Aesthetics to Follow|journal=Tulip|volume=13|issue=5|date=2022-11|page=66|passage=Soft girl makeup, as the name suggests is a pastel, sweet style that focuses on '''accentuating''' natural features with a signature element being blush and faux freckles.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To mark with a written accent.

